                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Reservation Suggestions Builder"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1773795839061"
                  },
                  "code": "RESERVATION_SUGGESTIONS_BUILDER",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "end_1773795839061",
                  "id": "1773359846851",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1773359846851_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "SuggestionMode: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.SuggestionMode}}\nData: {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_RESERVATION_SUGGESTIONS_LOOP.$currentItem}} \nExtract SupplySourceType and DemandSourceType from tables below :\n | DOCUMENT TYPE | DEMAND SOURCE TYPE    | DEMAND SOURCE TYPE ID |  \n            | ------------- | --------------------- | --------------------- |  \n            | Demand        | Sales order           | 2                     |  \n            | Demand        | Transfer order        | 8                     |  \n            | Demand        | Transfer order return | 18                    |  \n            | Demand        | Work order            | 5                     |  \n            | Demand        | Purchase order        | 1                     |  \n            | Demand        | Account               | 3                     |  \n            | Demand        | Account alias         | 6                     |  \n            | Demand        | Cycle count           | 9                     |  \n            | Demand        | User defined          | 13                    |\n\n| DOCUMENT TYPE | SUPPLY SOURCE TYPE         | SUPPLY SOURCE TYPE ID |  \n            | ------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------- |  \n            | Supply        | On hand                    | 13                    |  \n            | Supply        | Purchase order             | 1                     |  \n            | Supply        | Purchase order requisition | 17                    |  \n            | Supply        | Transfer order             | 8                     |  \n            | Supply        | Transfer order return      | 18                    |  \n            | Supply        | Work order                 | 5                     |\n\nCreate a list of suggestions.\nYour job is to match the earliest available supply for the item. First priority is for onhand, this can be used by multiple unique demands until it's depleted, in case there is not enough of onhand to satisfy the requested quantity, you should consider the earliest supply lines that are not onhand. You only recommend one suggestion per item. In the case that an item is mentioned more than once then we ensure to match them to different supplies. If number of unique supplies is not enough for all the item-demand combinations then we explicitly mention that only a subset satisfy the criteria and suggest accordingly.\nYou can only have one suggestion per demand\nSuggestion templates:\n- Reserve against onhand supply as that's the earliest available supply for the demand <DemandSourceType> <DemandSourceHeaderNumber> and line <DemandSourceLineNumber> for item <ItemNumber> of quantity <requestedQuantity> <UOM if present>(for DemandSourceType Work order we need to use `operation sequence number <operationSequence> instead of line <DemandSourceLineNumber>).\n- Reserving against supply <SupplySourceType> <SupplySourceHeaderNumber> as this is the earliest available supply at <ExpectedDeliveryDate> for the demand <DemandSourceType> <DemandSourceHeaderNumber> and line <DemandSourceLineNumber>(for DemandSourceType Work order we need to use `operation sequence number <operationSequence> instead of line <DemandSourceLineNumber>) for item <ItemNumber> quantity <requestedQuantity> <UOM if present>. (if supplysourcetype is transfer order then you need to add `line <SupplySourceLineNumber>` as well near the supply information).\n\n\nAfter selecting the suggestion for a demand line create a json with the following fields:\n{\n  \"DemandSourceHeaderNumber\": <DemandSourceHeaderNumber>,\n  \"DemandSourceLineNumber\": <DemandSourceLineNumber>,\n  \"OperationSequenceNumber\": <OperationSequenceNumber>,\n  \"DemandSourceTypeId\": <DemandSourceTypeId>,\n  \"SupplySourceTypeId\": <SupplySourceTypeId this will be 13 for onhand>,\n  \"SupplySourceHeaderNumber\": <SupplySourceHeaderNumber this will be null for onhand>,\n  \"SupplySourceLineNumber\": <SupplySourceLineNumber this will be null for onhand>,\n  \"RequestedQuantity\": <RequestedQuantity>(this should be minimum of RequestedQuantity/availability of onhand or other supply),\n  \"ExpectedDeliveryDate\": <ExpectedDeliveryDate>,\n  \"UOM\": <UOM>,\n  \"InventoryItemId\": <InventoryItemId>,\n  \"Suggestion\": <Suggestion for the line, if there is no eligible supply then you set it as `No eligible supply` and leave the supply fields blank>\n}\n\nNote: DO NOT show anything other than suggestions JSON.\nDO NOT match a supply and demand with different inventory item id.\nFinal output is an array of suggestion JSONs."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                }
              ],
              "rootNode": "start_1773795839061"
            },
            "loopType": "PARALLEL",
            "name": "Create Reservation Suggestions Loop"
