                  "code": "SUPPLY_SUGGESTION_BUILDER",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "end_1773797105700",
                  "id": "1773359608596",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1773359608596_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Data: {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_A_SUPPLY_SUGGESTION_LOOP.$currentItem}} \nExtract SupplySourceType from here:\n| DOCUMENT TYPE | SUPPLY SOURCE TYPE         | SUPPLY SOURCE TYPE ID |  \n            | ------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------- |  \n            | Supply        | On hand                    | 13                    |  \n            | Supply        | Purchase order             | 1                     |  \n            | Supply        | Purchase order requisition | 17                    |  \n            | Supply        | Transfer order             | 8                     |  \n            | Supply        | Transfer order return      | 18                    |  \n            | Supply        | Work order                 | 5                     |\n\nCreate a list of suggestions.\nYour job is to match the earliest available supply for the item. First priority is for onhand, this can be used by multiple unique reservations until it's depleted, in case there is not enough of it, you should consider the earliest supply lines. You only recommend one suggestion per item. In the case that an item is mentioned more than once then we ensure to match them to different supplies. If number of unique supplies is not enough for all the item-demand combinations then we explicitly mention that only a subset satisfy the criteria and suggest accordingly.\nYou can only have one suggestion per demand\nSuggestion templates:\n- Changing Supply to onhand as that's the earliest available supply, for the reservation <ReservationId> for item <ItemNumber> of quantity <requestedQuantity> <UOM if present>.\n- Changing supply to <SupplySourceType extract from the table> <SupplySourceHeaderNumber> as that's the earliest available supply at <ExpectedDeliveryDate>, for the reservation <ReservationId> for item <ItemNumber> quantity <requestedQuantity> <UOM if present>. (if supplysourcetype is transfer order then you need to add `line <SupplySourceLineNumber>` as well near the supply information).\n\nAfter selecting the suggestion for a reservation create a json with the following fields:\n{\n  \"ReservationId\": <ReservationId>,\n  \"SupplySourceTypeId\": <SupplySourceTypeId this will be 13 for onhand>,\n  \"SupplySourceHeaderNumber\": <SupplySourceHeaderNumber this will be null for onhand>,\n  \"SupplySourceLineNumber\": <SupplySourceLineNumber this will be null for onhand>,\n  \"RequestedQuantity\": <RequestedQuantity>,\n  \"UOM\": <UOM>,\n  \"DemandSourceHeaderNumber\": <DemandSourceHeaderNumber>,\n  \"DemandSourceLineNumber\": <DemandSourceLineNumber>,\n  \"OperationSequenceNumber\": <OperationSequenceNumber>,\n  \"DemandSourceTypeId\": <DemandType>,\n  \"ExpectedDeliveryDate\": <ExpectedDeliveryDate>,\n  \"ItemNumber\": <ItemNumber>,\n  \"InventoryItemId\": <InventoryItemId>,\n  \"Suggestion\": <Suggestion for the line, if there is no eligible supply then you set it as `No eligible supply` and leave the supply fields blank>\n}\n\nNote: DO NOT show anything other than suggestions JSON.\nFinal output is an array of suggestion JSONs."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "",
                  "type": "LLM"
                }
              ],
              "rootNode": "start_1773797105700"
            },
